  "market_context": "Price had been in a downtrend with lower lows, then failed to make a new lower low, signaling potential trend reversal. The analyst identified this structural shift as the trigger for drawing Fibonacci retracement from the swing low (0.6682) to the failed breakdown point (0.6818).",
  "key_observation": "Price formed a double bottom at the 0.5–0.618 Fibonacci Gold Zone (≈0.6727–0.6743), while RSI showed a higher low—confirming bullish regular divergence and validating the reversal setup.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify market structure failure—price failed to make a new lower low, indicating potential trend reversal and triggering Fibonacci retracement draw.",
    "Step 2: Draw Fibonacci retracement from the lowest swing (0.6682) to the point where structure broke (0.6818), identifying the 0.5 and 0.618 levels as the Gold Zone (≈0.6727–0.6743).",
    "Step 3: Observe price action at the Gold Zone: two touches forming a double bottom with a flat base, signaling rejection of lower prices.",
    "Step 4: Confirm with RSI: price made a second low near 0.6727 while RSI made a higher low, establishing a bullish regular divergence.",
    "Step 5: Enter long trade on rejection from the Gold Zone, with TP1 at prior swing high (0.6818), TP2 at -0.382 extension (≈0.6792), and TP3 at -0.618 extension (≈0.6810)."
  ],
  "outcome": "Trade reached TP1 (prior swing high) and continued to TP2 (-0.382 extension); partial profits taken, remainder trailed toward TP3. Confirmed profitable long move.",
  "lessons": "The highest-probability entries occur when Fibonacci Gold Zone confluence aligns with price action (double bottom) and momentum confirmation (RSI divergence). Never enter blindly—always require multiple confluences.",
